Assertions:
[BLADE] a member-list blade opens as a NEW blade appended to the stack, not replacing the condition-tree blade {OBSERVED}
[GRID] the blade's row count == $COUNTS[$GROUP_ONE] {OBSERVED}
[GRID] every rendered row's identity belongs to $GROUP_ONE's own membership (spot-check at least one row against a direct /api/members/search?groups=[$GROUP_ONE] response) {SPEC}

[GRID] blade row count == $COUNTS[$GROUP_SMALL] exactly {OBSERVED}
[GRID] blade row count != $TOTAL_UNFILTERED {OBSERVED}
[GRID] no rendered row belongs to a member outside $GROUP_SMALL, cross-checked against a direct /api/members/search?groups=[$GROUP_SMALL] response {SPEC}

[GRID] the blade shows a defined empty-state (e.g. an explicit 'no data' message), not an indefinite spinner or a blank panel {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no JS error is thrown while rendering the empty result set {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the header count badge is ABSENT for a zero-member group — it disappears rather than rendering '0'; that is the defined empty state, not a defect {OBSERVED}

[GRID] at least one rendered row has memberType Organization and at least one has memberType Contact {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the ticket's own text describes this blade as 'a filtered list of contacts'; record the Organization rows as SPEC-vs-OBSERVED drift, not necessarily a hard fail, unless the ticket is read as requiring exclusion {SPEC}
[DOM] each row's memberType is conveyed by an icon carrying a title tooltip and by nothing else — there is no text label column; this is the pre-existing member-list rendering shared with the root Contacts list (BL-A11Y-002 gap, recorded, not a fail of this blade) {OBSERVED}

[STATE] the unsaved description marker text is still present in the Promotion editor after the member-list blade is opened and closed {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the unsaved 'User group is' condition (with its selected group) is still present and still unsaved {OBSERVED}
[REL] the blade-stack depth immediately after closing the member-list blade equals the blade-stack depth immediately before clicking 'Show customers' (no net blade added or removed, so no duplicate Promotion blade and no stack reset) {OBSERVED}

[GRID] enumerate the row-level action control: record whether a menu opens and list EVERY item it offers {OBSERVED}  <- recording this is mandatory; an absent menu must be reported as absent, never left blank
[GRID] Delete is NOT among the items offered {SPEC}
[GRID] 'Manage' IS offered and opens the member record - the read-only mode suppresses the LIST's own mutating commands (Add / Delete / Invite), not navigation to a member; the stricter containment reading was raised and explicitly withdrawn by the product owner on 2026-09-15 {SPEC}

